 "FIGURE": "fig3_summary_rule_artefact",
 "CAPTION": "The summary rule, not the field. (a) Observed minus predicted cumulative radial profile at 15 radii. Over 116 historical mobile arms the largest standardised deviation is 0.64 and the largest difference 0.0038. The static curve rests on three arms and is shown for completeness only: it is not powered for a per-radius test, and its largest standardised deviation, 8.90, occurs where the absolute difference is no larger than at radii whose standardised deviation is below one. (b) The historical residual at three lattice sizes under the frozen median rule and under the mean rule. (c) A surrogate that draws particles independently from the predicted law and applies the same summary rule, with no lattice dynamics whatever, is already biased downwards under the median rule and nearly unbiased under the mean. (d) The surrogate does not account for the observed mobile dispersion; the full construction does.",
